WEBVTT

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.750
STREET INTERVIEW - ANNOYING BOSSES!

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.910
Today, we're here in Shibuya.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.620
Our topic is "annoying bosses."
Let's get to it!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.700
How about you, lady with the yellow fur?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.660
What kind of work do you do?

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.500
I'm an office worker.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.790
You have an annoying boss, right?

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.910
Well, yeah.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.250
What kind?

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.660
Well,

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.410
there's one who unloads work on me just
before it's time to leave for the day.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.950
That does happen, doesn't it?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.410
It's like,
"You could have asked me earlier!"

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.290
I see! Thanks for taking the time to...

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.500
And there's one who makes fun of me
just because I'm a woman,

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.790
even though he bends over backwards
for the girl who flatters him.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.450
And he works up a sweat from goofing off!

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.870
You seem to have a lot of complaints.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.290
Thank you very...

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.700
<i>I hope your ears are burning!</i>

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.500
<i>You lazy male chauvinist</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:09.370
<i>Waste of flesh!</i>

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:10.830
RAGE

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:01.830
<i>Actually, I was thinking I might</i>
<i>start a business here in Japan.</i>

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.500
<i>An imported goods store.</i>
<i>You want in, Retsuko?</i>

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.200
<i>Wow...</i>

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.660
<i>An imported goods store.</i>

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.290
<i>It sounds like a dream!</i>

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.580
<i>It's too alluring!</i>

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.250
What's this?
Retsuko, did something good happen?

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.620
Nothing in particular.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Really?

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.040
It's nothing.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.000
Really?

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:46.370
I can see a long, dark tunnel
through the back of your eyes.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.450
The meaning behind that smile is...

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.450
a release from darkness,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.290
freedom.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.620
<i>How is it that she can</i>
<i>accurately read my mind?</i>

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.080
<i>This middle-aged woman</i>
<i>is a rumor-spreading pro.</i>

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:04.120
<i>If she picks up the scent</i>
<i>that I might change jobs,</i>

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.700
<i>the rumor will spread</i>
<i>all over the company.</i>

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.500
I can't hide anything from you,
Mrs. Kabae!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.120
The truth is, I haven't been
able to poop for five days.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.950
-But this morning, it happened.
-You unplugged the long, dark tunnel?

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:22.910
That's right!

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.250
I knew it!

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.830
That's the face you were making.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.120
That was close.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:34.450
Oh, Retsuko.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.830
I heard your constipation cleared up.
Good for you.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.450
<i>It's already spreading...</i>

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.290
Also, I saw you...

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.500
on afternoon TV, in an interview
about "annoying bosses."

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.950
What are you talking about?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.250
<i>There was a mosaic over your face,</i>
<i>but it was you, wasn't it?</i>

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.200
Me, on TV?

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.540
No way! I haven't even been
to Shibuya recently!

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:02.580
Shibuya?

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.750
Did I mention Shibuya?

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.700
You did, not long ago.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.120
Is that right?

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.000
She looked just like you.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.830
Apparently so!

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.450
<i>Now I've done it!</i>

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.540
<i>I've been far too careless,</i>
<i>ever since I met with Puko.</i>

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.160
<i>I have to be careful.</i>

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.410
Retsuko!

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:43.870
Haida, what's wrong?

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.080
Retsuko! You...

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.950
Is it true you gave birth yesterday?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.250
-I heard it was a difficult delivery!
-Hey! When have I ever looked pregnant?

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.790
Fenneko, stop laughing!

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.790
I don't know where
or how the story got twisted,

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.370
but it was originally
a different story, so...

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.700
Is that right?

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.500
Oh, that was a scare.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.000
I see, now.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.660
So what was the story
before it got twisted?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.660
I said, stop laughing!

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.200
Young people have it good.
It looks like you're having fun.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.450
Retsuko...

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.200
a word...

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.910
Here! Here and here and here!

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.080
This is also wrong!

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.620
I'm sorry...

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.410
What's wrong?

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.660
You've been sluggish lately, haven't you?

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.910
I wonder what it is
you're showing up to work for.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.620
My job.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.870
Oh? I thought you were here to play.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.750
That's why you can make
this kind of face at work, isn't it?

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.950
Oh, it truly does look fun. How nice!

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.580
To think you get paid for playing!

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.250
<i>It's true that I'm the one</i>
<i>who made mistakes, but...</i>

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:09.040
Well, it was stupid of me
to ask you to do it.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.700
Because all you do is waste time!

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:15.830
<i>That wasn't my work to do</i>
<i>in the first place, it was yours.</i>

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:20.450
<i>Why am I putting up with this?</i>

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.040
Retsuko.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.830
Retsuko!

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.830
Are you listening?

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.080
If it's that big a problem...

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.660
shouldn't you have done it yourself
from the start?

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.950
Do you know what you're saying?

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.040
<i>I said it.</i>

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.700
<i>There's no going back.</i>

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.330
<i>No more being a serious, good girl.</i>

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:05.450
KARAOKE

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.290
<i>I said it.</i>

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.870
<i>I said it!</i>

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.540
<i>I really said it!</i>

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.750
<i>I am triumphant!</i>

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.870
You talked back to your boss?
That's great!

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.330
No...

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.540
It didn't feel very grown up.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:36.950
No, it's good! Good vibes.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:43.620
Hey, Puko. About what
you were saying the other day...

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:50.200
Where are you planning
to open the imported goods shop?

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:52.250
Oh... the shop?

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:53.870
That's...

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.370
Oh! Wait. I'll guess.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.040
Shimokitazawa!

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.910
It's not Sancha, is it?
That would be nice and close to me!

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:09.620
Then...?

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.120
There is no shop.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:16.330
Eh?

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.160
What I said. There's no shop.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.870
Sorry! Didn't I tell you?

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.040
Then... how...?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.700
Internet sales.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.580
I asked an acquaintance
to set up a website.

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:32.330
I can't risk unpaid rent
right off the bat, can I?

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.790
All I've got to do
is keep the stock at home.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.160
Of course, it would be nice
to get a shop in the future.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:41.660
What's wrong?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.910
What about the pay?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.950
There won't be much
until the business gets rolling.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.250
My monthly rent might be a problem.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:57.870
Why not move out of your apartment?
Your parents live nearby, don't they?

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.370
Welcome!

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:17.910
Oh, dear.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.950
Did something bad happen, Retsuko?

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:25.580
I've just learned about
the harshness of reality.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.830
Retsuko!

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.950
Oh, Tsunoda.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:37.200
Is it true that
you're leaving the company?

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.750
Why? Are you getting married?

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:43.040
Are you switching jobs?
Going on a journey of self-discovery?

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.950
Who did you hear that from?

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.080
From Kabae in Accounting, but...

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:53.120
Retsuko?

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.330
Kabae!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.370
You could at least show a reaction.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.580
My salary!

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.830
My monthly fixed costs!

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:23.450
What's wrong? Retsuko, calm down!

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:28.080
Please don't spread the rumor
that I'm quitting.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:36.000
Certainly, I may be a chatterbox, and
my ability to spread rumors is legendary.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.790
But I wouldn't spread
a bad rumor like that,

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.830
which would put you in a bad position.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.290
But... Tsunoda said...

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.580
I'm sorry!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.700
Tsunoda is the only one I told.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.830
Because you two are good friends, right?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.910
No, we're not that close.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.000
I heard it from Komiya.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:01.330
And I told Tsunoda.
That's all. That's the truth.

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:02.870
Komiya?

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.250
Why would Komiya say that...?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.830
It seems Director Ton wants
to have a word with you.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:20.540
ACCOUNTING DEPARTMENT

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:26.160
A fresh start...

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.370
It's a good sound, isn't it?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:35.830
These days, accounting work
is clickety-clacked into software.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.290
But I've never been good with computers.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:44.660
I'm calculating, with this abacus,

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:49.660
how much money this company
has invested in your education.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.040
<i>At the same time,</i>
<i>I was also doing math in my head.</i>

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:02.950
<i>I weighed my priceless dream</i>
<i>against a costly reality,</i>

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.250
<i>and the numbers were against me.</i>

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.700
I'm sorry... I can't, after all.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.700
Hey! Don't look so down!

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.160
I'm sorry.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.410
Come on. Why are you apologizing?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.950
It's OK.
You've got your own way of living.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.000
Hey,

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:30.370
do you know why someone irresponsible
like me can live on nothing but dreams?

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.160
Why?

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:40.660
It's thanks to reliable people like you
working hard and diligently paying taxes,

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.330
and keeping the economy
from tanking, right?

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:48.120
Sorry, but I need you to live responsibly,

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:52.080
so us blockheads can go
where the wind takes us.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.750
OK, today is my treat.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.080
All right!

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.580
This is quite an amount.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.250
The real question is...

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:21.910
Recently, you've been acting strange.

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:26.410
I have investigated this
using my years of experience.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.200
Komiya!

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:29.790
From the following sites...

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:33.080
A job changing site: "Seriously?
Isn't my monthly salary pathetic?"

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:36.450
A Q&A site: "How do letters of
resignation and retirement differ?"

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:40.540
An AMA: "I just turned in my letter
of resignation. Ask me anything!"

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.040
-Continuing on, a self...
-Enough. You can stop there.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:46.950
You remember those, don't you?

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:51.540
You "clinked" on all of those websites
on the internet, during overtime.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:52.790
It's "clicked"!

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.580
You clicked on them during overtime.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:59.950
You used a company device
to accesic... accesserate...

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:08.580
Your browsing history is easily tracked
by the network manager.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.080
You're planning to quit, aren't you?

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.750
What are you here to do?
To raise funds for self-employment?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.200
To look for a boyfriend
like you're at a singles party?

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.290
To "clink-clink" on this man and that man?

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.000
Click! Click!

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.540
Well, whatever it is...

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.410
You've screwed yourself over.

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.410
As of now,

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.700
I've got a new name for you.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:37.660
You're "Short-timer" now.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:40.580
<i>I'm finished!</i>

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.120
Subtitle translation: John Haguewood
